    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "· Around the World in Eighty Days ·",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "*Around the World in Eighty Days* (Le tour du monde en 80 jours) is an adventure novel by French author Jules Verne, published in 1873. It tells the legendary story of English gentleman Phileas Fogg and his servant Passepartout as they circumnavigate the globe in 80 days despite numerous obstacles. The cover design featured on the new Dior Book Tote is based on the hardcover edition released by French publisher Saint-Pierre in 2017, with a royal blue background, white ribbon border, and white typography. Its minimalist design complements the clean, structured silhouette of the Book Tote. Available in a wide range of items: large, medium, mini, clutch, passport cover, and magnetic card holder, plus a hot-air balloon-shaped charm.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
