    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "· The Very Hungry Caterpillar ·",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "*The Very Hungry Caterpillar* is a children's picture book by American author Eric Carle, published in 1969. It tells the story of a very hungry caterpillar who eats a variety of foods before transforming into a butterfly. The original artwork uses collage to showcase the layered beauty of nature, with die-cut holes representing the caterpillar's bites. The new Book Tote recreates the color layers with different colored embroidery threads, while the white circular hole on the back apple adds a playful touch. Available in medium and mini sizes, along with an apple-shaped coin purse, a red DIOR letter charm, and a caterpillar-themed charm. Parents can even pair them with their children for a matching set.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
