    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "· A Clockwork Orange ·",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The men's large Book Tote features the cover of British novelist Anthony Burgess's 1962 dystopian novella *A Clockwork Orange*. The story follows teenage thug Alex, who is imprisoned for violent crimes and subjected to the \"aversion therapy\" brainwashing, becoming a \"clockwork orange\" stripped of free will. It was famously adapted into a film by Stanley Kubrick. The cover selected for this collection was designed in 1972 by David Pelham, then art director at Penguin Books. It depicts the protagonist Alex as a \"gear-eyed man\" wearing a bowler hat, with bold, solid colors and aggressive geometric symbols creating a stark contrast. Reproduced on the bag, it maintains strong visual impact.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
